# Java Clean Code

SOLID baseline:
- Single Responsibility: one clear reason to change per class
- Open/Closed: extend behavior without invasive edits
- Liskov Substitution: subtype contracts preserve behavior assumptions
- Interface Segregation: small focused contracts
- Dependency Inversion: high-level behavior depends on abstractions

Operational guardrails:
- avoid duplicated business logic across use-cases/services
- avoid long `if/else` chains when strategy/polymorphism fits better
- keep methods short and intention-revealing
- keep side effects explicit and localized
- use comments only for non-obvious design decisions

Import discipline — ZERO FQN tolerance:
- **NUNCA** usar Fully Qualified Names (FQN) inline no código (ex.: `java.util.List<String>`, `org.springframework.stereotype.Service`). **Sempre** importar o tipo no bloco de imports e usar o nome simples no corpo da classe.
- Ao encontrar qualquer FQN inline durante trabalho em qualquer ficheiro (mesmo fora do escopo da task), **corrigir imediatamente**: adicionar o import e substituir pelo nome simples.
- Wildcard imports (`import java.util.*`) são proibidos — importar cada tipo individualmente.
- Imports não usados devem ser removidos (limpeza de passagem — ver rule `25-clean-code.mdc`).

Design checks:
- DRY without over-abstraction
- KISS over speculative generic frameworks
- YAGNI for non-required extensions
